Subject: [PATCH 3/6] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 3, patch 3;
 built on b80c68991 with series 2 applied): A GATE READS ALL IT IS ABOUT --
 THE VACUITY GATE (the seat's planted case PV24). The checker listed an assert
 between two literals 'for review', and the gate refused only a test with no
 assert and a tautology: a test whose only assert was 'assert 1 != 2' passed,
 and main has one by that name. And the scan read tests/ alone, never the
 arcs' own locks. THE CHECKER has a fourth class, CANNOT-FAIL: a test in which
 no assert can fail, each being made of hand-written literals alone, and true.
 It is decided by working the expression out (literals, their arithmetic and
 comparisons, an entry taken from one; never a call), so that 'assert False'
 under an 'if' and 'assert 1 == 0' are not in it; and a name counts as a
 literal only if it is bound once at the top of the test and used nowhere but
 in asserts, so that a flag set on two paths, or a list handed to a call, is
 not. One literal assert among real ones stays in the review queue, whose
 count does not move. THE GATE refuses the class, and reads every tracked
 lock: 303 test functions in 73 arcs' own files, where all four classes now
 apply and find nothing. On main the class finds 26 test functions, each read
 by this seat; they are held by name, as found, in CANNOT_FAIL_AS_FOUND, a
 ceiling that may only shrink. (Main counted 23 by a reading this seat does
 not have; three more that cannot fail call a builtin on literals and are
 outside the class, which stops at a call.) scan() returns what it always has.
 The lock: six tests added to tests/test_a_gate_reads_all_it_is_about.py, with
 eight shapes that must be refused and nine that must not; on the commit
 before, four fail, three of them because the gate passes. 0 of 19.

